			"Message": "Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Sky into Current",
			"SHA": "3f5152d3eb507aa4e88f5520a35233bda668abfb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-11T02:21:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				11
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Simplify Wind import paths and build config after Target restructuring\n\nThe Wind package's compiled output structure has been flattened, removing the\n`Element/Wind/Source` path segment from `Target/`. Update all Sky workbench\nentry points (Electron, BrowserProxy, Mountain, BrowserTest) and the Astro\nbundler config to reference the new shorter paths.\n\nAffected imports: SkyEvent, Bootstrap, Install, LandWorkbenchGlobal,\nTauriMainProcessService, and Extensions ChangeStream now resolve from\n`@codeeditorland/wind/Target/` directly (e.g., `Target/Effect/Bootstrap`\ninstead of `Target/Element/Wind/Source/Effect/Bootstrap`).\n\nThe `@vite-ignore` comments on dynamic imports are no longer needed and are\nremoved. The external function in astro.config.ts is simplified: Wind Target\nis no longer explicitly externalized since its new flat structure avoids the\nprevious resolution conflicts. A new `ResolveOutputVSCodeInternals` Vite plugin\nhandles symlink-cycle imports from `@codeeditorland/output/Target/Microsoft/VSCode/`.\nThe `vite-plugin-top-level-await` polyfill is disabled in bundled profiles\nwhere VS Code workbench size crashes the NAPI Rust binding.",
			"SHA": "84a4010c90c392df4a4783e19204cbf8ac3c9448"
		},
